        '6-8', $q$The Garden Behind the School$q$, $q$(1) Last spring, the empty lot behind Harmon Middle School became a community garden. (2) At first, only a few neighbors showed up on Saturdays to pull weeds and haul away broken bricks. (3) More than thirty families had signed up for raised beds of their own. (4) Each family agreed to water its plot twice a week and to share any extra vegetables with the local food pantry. (5) My cousin has a small garden in her backyard, and she mostly grows roses.

(6) The garden soon changed the neighborhood in ways nobody had expected. (7) Older residents began teaching younger ones how to save seeds and turn food scraps into rich compost. (8) Students from Harmon used the beds to measure plant growth for their science projects. (9) People who had lived on the same street for years finally learned each other's names. (10) The lot that once collected trash now grows tomatoes, beans, and friendships.$q$, 'draft')
