   $q$Read the paragraph: "(1) Walking to school has real benefits for students. (2) A morning walk wakes up the body and the brain before the first class. (3) Walkers also get time to talk with friends on the way. (4) Many school buses are painted a bright shade of yellow. (5) Finally, walking produces no exhaust, so it helps keep the air clean." Which sentence does not belong?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Sentence 4","is_correct":true},{"text":"Sentence 3","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"removes-supporting-detail"},{"text":"Sentence 2","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"removes-supporting-detail"},{"text":"Sentence 5","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"removes-supporting-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Sentence 4$q$, $q$Every other sentence gives a benefit of walking to school, but sentence 4 describes the color of buses, which does not support the main idea. Sentence 5 belongs because clean air is another benefit, and "Finally" marks it as the last one.$q$, 'draft', null)
