   $q$Read: "Practicing scales helps pianists move their fingers quickly. ____, running drills helps soccer players react faster on the field." Which transition best shows that the second sentence makes a similar point?$q$, $q$[{"text":"In the same way,","is_correct":true},{"text":"Instead,","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"replacement-for-similarity"},{"text":"As a result,","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"cause-for-similarity"},{"text":"On the contrary,","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contrast-for-similarity"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$In the same way,$q$, $q$Both sentences describe practice that builds speed in a skill, so "In the same way" shows the comparison. "As a result" is wrong because a pianist's scales do not cause soccer players to react faster.$q$, 'draft', null)
