  ('f29b24ef-a562-59bf-b9b9-ef8b14067d09', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g8-paragraph-transitions'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Read the sentences: (A) For one thing, it would let students walk to school safely. (B) The town should build a footbridge over Miller Creek. (C) It would also connect two neighborhoods that are now cut off from each other. (D) Most important, it would give fire trucks a faster route across town. Which sentence should come first in a paragraph built from these sentences?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Sentence D","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"detail-as-topic"},{"text":"Sentence C","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"detail-as-topic"},{"text":"Sentence A","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"detail-as-topic"},{"text":"Sentence B","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Sentence B$q$, $q$Sentence B states the main claim, and the word "it" in the other sentences refers back to the footbridge it names. Sentence A cannot come first because "For one thing" and "it" both depend on a claim that has not been stated yet.$q$, 'draft', null)
