  ('ab896dfe-7281-56da-b2b4-e883d2ed161f', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g8-paragraph-transitions'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Read the sentences: (A) That vapor rises and cools high in the sky. (B) The sun warms the water in oceans and lakes, turning some of it into vapor. (C) Eventually, the droplets grow heavy enough to fall as rain or snow. (D) As it cools, the vapor forms tiny droplets that gather into clouds. Which is the most logical order for these sentences?$q$, $q$[{"text":"B, A, D, C","is_correct":true},{"text":"B, D, A, C","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-reference-cues"},{"text":"A, B, D, C","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-reference-cues"},{"text":"B, A, C, D","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-reference-cues"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$B, A, D, C$q$, $q$Sentence B creates the vapor, A says "That vapor" rises and cools, D tells what happens "As it cools," and C says "the droplets" fall. Order B, D, A, C is wrong because D describes cooling before A explains that the vapor rises and cools.$q$, 'draft', null)
