   $q$A paragraph begins, "Our town once had no place for teenagers to gather after school." The third sentence is "Today, the center is open five afternoons a week and full of students." Which sentence best fits between them?$q$, $q$[{"text":"In addition, the town has two public parks and a pool.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"addition-off-topic"},{"text":"Many teenagers enjoy playing board games with their friends.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-bridge"},{"text":"Two years ago, parents and students turned an empty store into a youth center.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The new youth center is planned to open sometime next year.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-sequence"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Two years ago, parents and students turned an empty store into a youth center.$q$, $q$The missing sentence must explain how the town went from having no place to having "the center," and only the correct choice introduces the center and when it began. The sentence saying it will open next year contradicts the third sentence, which says the center is already open.$q$, 'draft', null)
